# Predator Detection Network Project
## Vision: Distributed AI Wildlife Monitoring with Autonomous Drone Investigation

### Project Goal

Develop a scalable wildlife monitoring system that combines:

- Ground-based AI camera nodes
- LoRa communications
- Central command and control
- Autonomous drone investigation
- Solar-powered charging stations
- Future multi-drone capability

The system will continuously monitor for predators such as possums, cats, hedgehogs, rats and stoats, then dispatch a drone to investigate and verify detections.

---

# System Architecture

```text
Ground Camera Nodes
        │
        ▼
AI Detection
(Motion + YOLO)
        │
        ▼
LoRa Network
        │
        ▼
Central Command Server
        │
        ▼
Launch Decision Engine
        │
        ▼
Autonomous Drone
        │
        ▼
Perch Station / Charging Dock
```

---

# Core Concept

Traditional drones patrol continuously:

```text
Fly
Hover
Battery depleted
Return
```

This wastes significant energy.

Instead:

```text
Ground cameras detect activity
↓
Drone launched only when needed
↓
Drone investigates location
↓
Drone lands on perch station
↓
Motors off
↓
Long-duration observation
↓
Returns for charging
```

Ground sensors become the detectors.

The drone becomes the investigator.

